VeridianOS: linguist: define StatisticalData before its meta-type is checked

GCC 16 reported, for the host qttools build, in linguist's
mocs_compilation.cpp: "statistics.h:12: defining 'StatisticalData', which
previously failed to be complete in a SFINAE context
[-Wsfinae-incomplete]". messagemodel.h only forward-declared
StatisticalData but uses it in the statsChanged() signals of MessageModel
and MultiDataModel; the moc code for those classes (included earlier in
mocs_compilation.cpp than moc_statistics.cpp) asks QMetaType whether the
type is complete, gets "no", and statistics.h then defines it in the same
translation unit. The answer to that question must not change within a
program (the meta-type information would differ between translation
units), so this is worth fixing rather than a cosmetic warning.

The struct moves unchanged into a new header, statisticaldata.h, which
both messagemodel.h (instead of the forward declaration) and statistics.h
include, so the type is complete wherever the signal is declared. The new
header is listed with the other linguist sources in CMakeLists.txt. No
behaviour change.

